Author: Ryan Jiang

Description

This project implements a simple Unix shell in C supporting
interactive and batch modes. Features include built-in commands
(cd, pwd, which, exit), external command execution using fork()
and execv(), input/output redirection (<, >, >>), multiple pipes,
wildcard expansion, comments, and exit status reporting.

Compilation

Compile: make
Run interactively: ./mysh
Run batch file: ./mysh BatchTest.txt
Run batch stdin: ./mysh < BatchTest.txt
Clean: make clean

Testing

Testing was performed using both interactive and batch modes.

1. Built-ins: Tested pwd, cd, which, and exit with valid and
   invalid arguments.
2. External commands: Tested echo, ls, true, false, and invalid
   commands to verify execution and exit status reporting.
3. Redirection: Tested <, >, >>, including built-in redirection
   and file creation.
4. Pipelines: Tested two and multiple commands, built-ins in
   pipelines, and exit within a pipeline.
5. Wildcards: Tested prefix, suffix, directory patterns, hidden
   files, and unmatched patterns.
6. Comments: Tested inline and full-line comments.
7. Errors: Tested invalid pipes, missing filenames, and
   continued execution after syntax errors.
8. Batch mode: Tested file arguments, redirected stdin, and
   commands without a final newline.
